<title>USA: Sears completes Advantis sale.</title>
<headline>Sears completes Advantis sale.</headline>
<dateline>HOFFMAN ESTATES, Ill. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co said Thursday it completed the previously announced sale of its 30 percent equity interest in Advantis, the U.S. data network services arm of the IBM Global Network, to International Business Machines Corp.</p>
<p>Prior to the sale, Advantis was 70 percent owned by IBM.</p>
<p>Sears said it will record an after-tax gain from this sale, after contractually required distributions to third parties, of approximately $90 million, or $0.23 a share.</p>
<p>Advantis was formed by Sears and IBM in 1992 to provide network, data processing and value-added telecommunications serviceds to customers based in the U.S.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
